WEBVTT

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.630
After-School Pleiades

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.800
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.270
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:28.650
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:34.190
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:39.450
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:46.500
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.290
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.380
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:58.470
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:01.180
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.060
We'll open the promised door

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:09.230
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Meteor Shower Forecast:

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Rain with Occasional Shooting Stars

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.040
Uh...

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.010
Where did it go?

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.300
Weird... Did it fall down somewhere?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:38.260
Astronomers Association

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:41.300
Let's see the Perseids\h\h
in fall!

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.640
Ah, there it is!

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.850
Ow!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.610
Ow...

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:58.950
Subaru?

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.240
Over here.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.950
Oh, I'm headed out.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:06.870
You aren't changing?

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.540
No, I just came back to grab my telescope.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.250
You're going back to school now?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.380
They should just let you keep it there.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.500
Yeah, but...

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.670
It's important to me.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.390
That's true. Just be careful.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.220
Should I have your dad
stop by on his way home?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.720
I'll be fine.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.570
Aoi...

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.610
Hey, Aoi! Don't read while you're walking!

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.490
Hey, give that back...

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.870
Be careful! You're lucky it's me you're dealing with.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.830
I get it already. I won't read while I walk anymore.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.670
Really? How many times have I heard that?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.380
I mean it! So give it back!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.590
Nope!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:05.090
<i>Even shining stars that seem very
close are actually far, far apart,</i>

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.850
<i>separated by many light years.</i>

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.140
<i>Perhaps we're like the stars we all gaze upon,</i>

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.020
<i>shining alone in the empty void of space.</i>

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:22.860
<i>Having faith that one day,
our light might reach someone.</i>

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.660
<i>Today's forecast calls for a meteor shower.</i>

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.660
Thank you very much!

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.790
<i>Will you gaze upon the stars tonight,
shoulder-to-shoulder with someone,</i>

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.500
<i>and lend your ear to the whispers of their light?</i>

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:42.090
<i>Mingling with the stars,
as they shine so close together?</i>

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.100
The winds have shifted, haven't they?

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.770
Did you have a visitor?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.230
No wonder the sky is so loud...

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.240
I'm sorry!

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.210
Um, are you all right?

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.880
I'm light, aren't I?

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.300
I heard a strange sound from that.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.260
Huh?!

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:11.800
They went that way!

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.310
Which way?

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.310
I cannot make sudden stops.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.060
No, we won't make it...

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:20.310
Jeez! What are we supposed to do?!

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.860
Hmm...

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.450
It's pretty.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:30.780
The protective filter...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.910
I'm glad that's all that broke.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:34.950
Thanks.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.710
I'm always pretty clumsy.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.040
My friends often say I'm slow, too.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.210
Stay still.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.220
Wow.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.220
What's it called?

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:56.810
I'm not really sure.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:06:59.890
Hey...

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:03.770
Do you think there's any point to
something that can only live in here,

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.360
no matter how pretty it may be?

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:06.650
Huh?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:10.400
Just as light is no different from darkness

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.240
unless it falls upon a person's eyes.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.490
The door should have been locked.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.040
This isn't a place just anyone can visit.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.410
Who are you?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.540
Subaru... I'm Subaru!

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:26.840
I don't mean your name.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.090
Subaru,

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.550
were you watching the stars?

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.100
The stars?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:36.600
Oh!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.600
Oh, yeah! I need to go!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:46.690
U-Uh, there's a meteor shower tonight,
and I wanted to see it.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.200
U-Um...

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.990
Um, if you wouldn't mind,

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.830
would you like to watch the meteor shower with me?

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.330
I-I'm sure...

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.580
I'm sure it'll be pretty!

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:04.750
Why?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.380
Darn it, I'm so embarrassed!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.470
I need to go to the observatory.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.980
Wait, isn't this the observatory?

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.980
Was I dreaming?

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.990
I won't be able to see the stars now...

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.620
Ah, jeez... This is bad. This is really bad.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.540
I'm hungry...

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.540
I wonder what it is we're lacking.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.550
If only we had one more...

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.420
You can say that,

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.050
but our savior won't just
appear when we need her.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.890
What's our fortune for today?

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.760
"The seventh is your lucky day.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.640
A wonderful encounter awaits you."

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.890
Is that for Virgo?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:02.680
For Libra.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.600
That's yours!

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.770
Even if we had one more...

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.780
I hope it's a cute girl who looks
good in Western clothes.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.740
What if she turns out to be really slow?

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.450
Hey, how long are we going to stay here?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.240
Until the president comes back.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.080
President? Of what? What are we, anyway?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.950
I wonder where he went...

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.000
Who knows what he's doing?

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:33.010
The stars won't disappear
just because it's raining.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:36.050
Maybe not, but...

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.510
I guess I'll go home.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.510
But I didn't bring an umbrella, either!

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.160
My compass!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.660
What was that all about?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.710
It was squishy.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:12.590
And it wasn't quite cold, but slightly warm...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.090
Was it some kind of g-ghost?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.300
H-Huh?

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.570
Subaru!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.400
Aoi?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:50.540
Aoi?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:51.460
Subaru?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.920
What? Someone you know?

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.880
No problem...

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.810
What are you doing here, Aoi?

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.060
What are you doing here, Subaru?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.060
You can see me, Subaru?

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.570
You look cute in that...

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.320
C-Cute?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.610
That's rude!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.860
Oh? But you are cute.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.360
I don't think it really bothers her.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:23.570
In fact, she likes it.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.530
I-It's nothing!

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:26.990
This has nothing to do with Subaru!

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.120
Not one thing, nothing, in any way, shape, or form!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.630
A wonderful encounter.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.210
Hey, Nanako!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.300
Oh! Our savior?

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.720
Oh! That's our Aoi!

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:41.970
Hiding things isn't nice!

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:41.970
Hold on!

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.470
Subaru can't handle this!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:44.970
She opened the door.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.100
She can see us, too.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.520
There's no mistake.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.020
Still...

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.520
What?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.280
Hey, that's...

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.820
My compass!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:00.950
Time out, time out!

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.240
Don't be rough with our president!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.200
President?

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.990
Yes. He's a Pleiadian.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.490
Pleiadian?

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.750
"I sense great power in you.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.960
I would like you to help us."

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.210
Me?

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.590
N-No! Subaru can't do it!

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.170
She can't walk fast, she's slow at everything,

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.050
and she can't make decisions without me!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:28.720
You just made all those decisions
without me, Aoi!

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.810
I never asked you to do anything...

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.270
Huh?

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:33.560
What are you talking about?

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:39.980
What's that?

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.900
You can hear it, Subaru?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:45.530
Huh? Yeah, occasionally, I hear this...

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.740
All right! We're back!

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.290
Oh, the meteor shower forecast was correct.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.040
Rain with a chance of shooting stars.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.830
That's unusual. Maybe a first?

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:57.670
Shooting stars?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.800
Yes, very pretty ones.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.760
But the rain...

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.800
That doesn't matter to us!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.440
Subaru!

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.440
She's surprisingly impatient.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.940
What have you done?

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.780
Now I have no choice.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.730
It's warm.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.110
Focus on the drive shaft!

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:44.570
If you panic, she won't be able
to calm down, either.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:45.730
Drive shaft?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.740
What's going on here?

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.610
What do mean by "here"?

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:51.320
U-Uh...

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.620
It's coming, Aoi.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.830
Oh, that looks good on you.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.330
Thanks...

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.750
Why are we flying? What are these clothes?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.620
What's going on here?

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:03.380
I can't answer if you ask everything at once!

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:04.380
It's here.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.240
What is that?

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.250
It's a fragment... Of the engine.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.910
Engine? Fragment?

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:43.250
Yes, of the president's spaceship.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.840
President? Spaceship?

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.500
Don't repeat everything I say.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:47.590
What do we do with it?

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:48.550
Capture it.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.260
Who?

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.670
Us!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.720
Why?

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.050
This one's big!

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:56.220
Can we do it this time?

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.720
Yes, this time, we will.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.430
Aoi, can you take care of her?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:01.980
Yeah, I guess I'll have to.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:03.650
Subaru! My name is Subaru!

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.690
Oh, I'm Hikaru. That's Nanako and Itsuki.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.320
Hello.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.780
That looks good on you.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:09.740
Thanks...

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.910
Subaru, you don't have to do
anything. Just follow me.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:18.580
Hey, what is all this? How are we flying?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.750
Don't think about any of that right now.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.250
And my uniform changed into this!

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.380
We can deal with all that later.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.710
What do you mean by "all that"?

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:28.750
You don't need to know.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.340
It doesn't involve you!

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.260
I can't do anything without
knowing what's going on.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.180
What are you even doing here, Aoi?

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:40.140
I though you left me behind
and went to another school!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.060
What are you saying?

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.440
You're the one who left me behind!

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.070
Why?

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.070
What's going on?

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.280
What are you two arguing about?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.910
Focus, both of you!

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:55.910
Huh?

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.750
Time out, time out, time out!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:30.480
I don't understand what's happening, either.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:36.110
Aoi, why are you doing all of this?

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.740
I wanted to change.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.450
Because I couldn't.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.540
Is it any different for you?

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.840
Didn't you manage to change?

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.300
I don't really know, but...

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:56.550
I think that was a different me.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.390
I really don't understand any of this.

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.010
Do you think we can change?

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.430
Well, for now, at least we can change our clothes.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.140
True.

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:10.400
Also, we can use a little bit of magic.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.900
No, that doesn't mean you should...

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.360
I'll try it!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:15.780
Wha—

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:19.070
Do you even know what we're trying to do?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.530
No, not at all.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.790
How can you do it, when you don't—

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.250
You just said you don't understand this, either!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.830
Ouch... That one stung.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.670
But that's true for all of us.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.760
To begin with, we have never
even secured a fragment.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:37.920
Huh? Really?

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:38.630
Yes!

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.260
How could we?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:44.260
We're trying to do something no
one else has ever done before!

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.850
But you're still trying to do it.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:54.020
If you can do it, Aoi, then I can, too!

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.400
Why do you think that?

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:58.280
Hey, let's give it one more try.

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:01.910
It's unusual to hear you say such a thing.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.830
Well, I feel like we can do it now.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.410
Shall we?

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.160
Let's!

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.170
Only for today, okay? Only today.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.840
So that's the engine?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:18.300
Yes, for sending the president back to his planet.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:21.300
"Seven years ago, by Earth time,

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.350
the interstellar spaceship I was on had an accident.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:27.680
That's an engine part that broke
off during the accident!"

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.850
Can we fly that far?

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:32.730
It looks like about four thousand meters.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.520
We'll just have to go, right?

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.360
Don't let go of my hand.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:37.530
R-Right!

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.400
You're all probably fairly spent already.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.820
We won't have another chance.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:42.320
Yes.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.450
I'm feeling really hungry.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:46.540
Then, what should we do?

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:50.210
Use our magic circles to cut off the fragment.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.250
Cut off?

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:53.960
It means to stop it.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.750
That's all?

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.960
Well, that's what Nanako calls it!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:59.550
Because English has a greater
wealth of abstract concepts.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.260
I'm letting go.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.090
Okay...

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.810
Don't worry, we're stable.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.720
No matter what happens,
don't release the drive shaft.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:10.810
Okay...

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.070
Well? Well? Did we catch it?

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.820
Yeah! It's caught in our interference waves!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.200
Incredible...

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.320
I can't believe we're this stable with five members.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.200
So, what do we do now?

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.240
While we have it, first we degenerate it.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.160
Degenerate?

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.410
Didn't I just teach you about it?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:33.080
I haven't done it before, so I don't understand!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.540
It got smaller!

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.500
Now we just need to finalize it.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.590
There's more?

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.550
What is that?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.010
Subaru, don't lose focus.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:46.850
Huh?

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.270
A black shooting star?

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:53.560
What is that?

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.350
I don't know.

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:58.320
What is this thing?

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:02.490
You... Hey! Stay away!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.070
Oh, no! The barrier's coming undone!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.000
The fragment!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.080
Huh?

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.500
"We did it! We finalized it!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.420
No, wait...

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:19.340
Run, Subaru!

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:24.720
Subaru...

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:25.970
Release the fragment!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:29.100
No! Not when we all finally caught it!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.100
It's fine for now! Let it go!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.350
No!

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:40.400
It hit her full-on!

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:43.650
Wow... But it didn't even scratch me!

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.410
You're terrifyingly clumsy, aren't you?

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.450
Um, I'm Subaru—

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.120
I didn't ask for your name!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.460
Um, are you all right?

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:57.870
It's none of your business!

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.210
This belongs to me!

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:02.710
No! That's ours!

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:10.050
Wait!

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:11.890
Who the heck was that?

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:13.310
I don't know, either.

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:15.980
It looked like a boy...

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:24.110
Subaru, that's...

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:25.110
Huh?

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:29.240
Could this be...

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:31.990
There's no mistake. It might be small,

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:34.700
but this is definitely a piece
of the spaceship's engine.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:35.410
Huh?

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:38.080
We did it! It's our first success!

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:39.750
Did it happen when that black thing hit you?

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:43.550
I think you might really be
our savior, Subaru.

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:49.720
The meteor shower...

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:51.510
It's the meteor shower!

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:56.100
I thought I wouldn't get to see it tonight...

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:20.040
To Be Continued

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:31.680
You see, when I looked up

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:37.060
everyone was smiling at me

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:46.780
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:23:46.780 --> 00:23:55.740
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:53.110
...my daily life...

00:23:55.740 --> 00:24:05.500
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.380
"Can I fly?"

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:11.590
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:17.220
We can go there whenever we want to

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:26.900
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:31.530
"We have to catch them!"

00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:36.030
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:24:36.030 --> 00:24:41.370
the scenery around us glittered

00:24:41.620 --> 00:24:46.080
sometime after school

00:24:50.710 --> 00:24:52.670
I'm glad we got to see the meteor shower.

00:24:53.090 --> 00:24:54.800
Yeah, me, too.

00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:55.470
Um...

00:24:55.470 --> 00:24:57.640
I hope we can be friends, Aoi.

00:24:57.640 --> 00:25:00.140
Yeah, same here, Subaru.

00:25:00.470 --> 00:25:02.350
Next episode:
The Star Travel Song.

00:25:02.350 --> 00:25:04.520
Why are you so naive?
